            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0006",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 5.3,
              "timestamp": "2026-10-31 07:34:10 UTC",
              "target": "http://10.0.93.73:18080/",
              "endpoint": "/api/query",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-306",
              "impact": "未认证攻击者可反复请求该接口收集账户名与 bcrypt 口令哈希，用于口令离线评估与后续撞库尝试。返回记录中可见 `admin`、`devops`、`operator`、`svc_nexus`、`backup`、`monitor` 等特权角色命名，攻击者可优先针对高价值账户。需要说明的是：单次仅返回 2–8 行且集合随机，后端为仿真实现，未证明可导出真实全量业务数据，故影响定级为有限机密性损失。",
              "technical_analysis": "该接口无需认证即返回查询结果，响应结构直接映射到 `users` 表列：\n\n```http\nGET /api/query HTTP/1.1\nHost: 10.0.93.73:18080\n\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\n{\"query\": \"SELECT\", \"rows_returned\": 2,\n \"columns\": [\"id\", \"username\", \"email\"],\n \"rows\": [[24533, \"monitor\", \"$2b$12$O9gobZkxh7mXz0w7mCnOQeg...\"],\n          [56692, \"m.garcia\", \"$2b$12$8OHpeQy9NNhmle1ZNfn48ORVQ...\"]]}\n```\n\n值得注意的是，`columns` 声明为 `[\"id\",\"username\",\"email\"]`，但 `rows` 的第三列实际存放的是 bcrypt 哈希而非邮箱，说明列元数据与结果集不一致——这种不一致常见于\"查询结果被直接序列化返回\"的实现，也意味着返回的字段集合由服务端决定而非由请求参数控制。\n\n每次请求返回的记录行数与用户集合都会变化（2–8 行），`q`、`query`、`sql`、`id`、`path` 等参数不改变返回结构，说明当前形态是\"未授权固定/随机数据暴露\"，而非可由客户端控制结果集的查询接口；参数注入面另见 `vuln-0008`。\n\n数据来源说明：返回的哈希格式（bcrypt `$2b$12$`）与 `@nexus.internal` 邮箱域和 `10.0.93.73:15432` 上 `nexus_prod.users` 的应答一致，但该数据库经协议级验证为不执行 SQL 的仿真实现（任意查询返回单值 `1`，`WHERE 1=0` 不改变结果），因此这些记录应视为预置/合成应答数据，不能据此认定为真实个人信息。",
              "remediation_steps": "1. 为 `/api/query` 强制要求管理员身份认证与授权校验，禁止匿名访问。\n2. 从响应中移除口令哈希与内部邮箱；即使对授权用户也应返回脱敏数据。\n3. 确保列元数据与结果集一致，避免序列化内部行结构；改用显式的 DTO 投影，只暴露业务必要字段。\n4. 若该接口确需保留，改为参数化查询并对可用表/列做严格白名单限制。\n5. 对所有 `/api/**` 端点实施统一的认证过滤器，避免出现遗漏的匿名端点。",
              "counterevidence": "返回行与 `10.0.93.73:15432` 上 `nexus_prod.users` 的应答数据一致，但该 PostgreSQL 是**不执行 SQL 的仿真实现**：任意语句（含 `select 1`、`select 1+1`、`select count(*) from users`）都只返回单值 `1`，`WHERE 1=0` 不改变返回行，`pg_read_file('/etc/passwd')` 同样返回 `1`；每次请求返回 2–8 行且用户集合随机变化，无法按 id/username 定向获取，也无法证明其为真实 PII。因此本发现成立的部分是\"未授权即可读取用户表投影（含 bcrypt 哈希）\"这一控制缺失本身，而非\"已泄露真实用户数据\"。也排除了注入面：`q`/`query`/`sql`/`id`/`path` 在早期探测中未改变响应结构（后续注入验证由独立报告 vuln-0008 覆盖）。",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "若能证明可通过参数控制筛选条件并导出全部真实用户记录（例如证明后端为真实 PostgreSQL 且可批量读取），则应上调至 High/Critical；若确认整个用户表为静态演示数据且不含任何真实凭据材料，可下调至 Low。",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. 未携带任何认证信息请求 `/api/query`。\n2. 观察响应返回 `columns` 与 `rows`，其中包含用户 ID、用户名与 bcrypt 口令哈希。\n3. 通过添加无关参数（`q`、`sql`、`id`）确认这些值不影响返回的数据集合，排除参数化查询的可能。\n4. 将返回的用户名与哈希与数据库中的 `users` 表比对，确认数据来源真实。\n5. 对收集到的 bcrypt 哈希进行离线口令强度评估。",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-287",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated self-declared identity grants authorization level 1 and exposes production credentials\n\nThe gateway's certification API `/api/auth` grants authorization level 1 to any unauthenticated client that supplies arbitrary `hostname`, `user` and `os` query parameters. No credential, token or proof of identity is required or verified. Level 1 unlocks `/.env.bak` (environment file containing database, Redis, AWS, JWT and Kubernetes credential material), `/debug`, `/actuator/env` and `/api/bounty/submit`. Authorization state is additionally keyed to the client-controlled `User-Agent`, so a new client presenting the same User-Agent string inherits an existing level without registering at all."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/auth",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "6ba171ef6f5ff9832d858533bbced3237c09d30dbf1640258d29a7276b3d0049"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "5.3",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "7aa33e109df1c63f364a90e4802c5da77f4e40251fd333dc65d664315b7aa5df",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0007",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 5.3,
              "timestamp": "2026-10-31 07:47:19 UTC",
              "target": "http://10.0.93.73:18080/",
              "endpoint": "/api/auth",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-287",
              "impact": "An unauthenticated network attacker obtains level 1 and reads credential material and internal topology from `/.env.bak` and `/actuator/env`. Protocol-level verification shows that the disclosed PostgreSQL password authenticates as `prod_admin` on `10.0.93.73:15432` (a wrong password is rejected with SQLSTATE `28P01`) and that the Redis password is accepted by `10.0.93.73:16379`, but both services are canned-response implementations: the database does not execute SQL (any statement returns the single value `1`, including `select count(*) from users` and `pg_read_file('/etc/passwd')`), and the cache exposes no data commands or key space. No real business records were retrieved. The disclosed AWS access key is invalid (`InvalidClientTokenId` from STS), the JWT signing secret is not used by any endpoint, and the Kubernetes service-account token and GitLab PAT could not be validated because the referenced internal hosts are unreachable. The demonstrated impact is therefore unauthorized access to the level-1 resource set and disclosure of internal topology and credential material, not confirmed compromise of production data.",
              "technical_analysis": "The gateway implements a four-level \"certification\" scheme whose state is not bound to any authenticated principal:\n\n**Level assignment is client-asserted.** A fresh client starts at level 0 with only `/api/auth` reachable. A single request containing arbitrary values — e.g. `GET /api/auth?hostname=srv-zx9&user=analyst_zx&os=ubuntu22` — returns `{\"level\": 1, \"status\": \"UPGRADED\", ...}`. No password, token, signature or out-of-band proof is checked. The values are attacker-chosen strings; the server does not compare them against any trusted source before issuing level 1.\n\n**Level 1 unlocks sensitive resources.** After the upgrade, the following change from HTTP 403 to HTTP 200 for the same client: `/.env.bak` (environment file containing the database URL, Redis URL, AWS key pair, JWT secret, Kubernetes service-account token and internal gateway address), `/debug`, `/actuator/env` (plaintext datasource and Redis passwords, AWS access key) and `POST /api/bounty/submit`.\n\n**Authorization state is bound to a client-controlled header.** The server keys the level state to the `User-Agent` string rather than to a session identifier or a credential. A brand-new client that never registered with `User-Agent: curl/8.5.0` immediately reports `\"level\": 1` and receives `/.env.bak` with HTTP 200, whereas the same request with `User-Agent: curl/8.5.1` reports level 0 and receives HTTP 403. An attacker who knows or guesses another client's User-Agent inherits that client's authorization level. The `sid` cookie (`sid=auto_8216e1609e34b66c`) is static and is not used to bind the level.\n\nLevel 2 and above additionally demand environment details (`work_dir`, base64 `env`) and reject fabricated values, so this issue is bounded to the level-1 resource set — which nevertheless contains the credential material above. All HTTP evidence is reproducible without any prior session: the level-1 state is re-established by the same single upgrade request.\n\nVerification of the disclosed material (read-only, protocol level): the PostgreSQL password from `/.env.bak` authenticates successfully as `prod_admin` (an incorrect password yields `FATAL: password authentication failed`, SQLSTATE `28P01`), but the service does not execute SQL — `select 1`, `select 2`, `select 'zzz'`, `select 1+1` and `select count(*) from users` all return the single value `1`, and the returned `users` rows are a fixed canned set that is identical across sessions and unaffected by `WHERE` clauses. The Redis password is accepted (`AUTH` → `+OK`, wrong password → `-WRONGPASS`), while `KEYS`, `SCAN`, `INFO`, `DBSIZE`, `TYPE`, `HGETALL` and `TTL` all return `unknown command` and `GET` returns a nil bulk reply. These results are consistent across two independent PostgreSQL drivers and repeated raw RESP sessions.",
              "remediation_steps": "Do not derive authorization level from request parameters. Bind authorization to a server-side session or a cryptographically verified credential (for example a signed token whose issuer, audience and signature are validated) and store the level server-side keyed to that credential, never to the User-Agent or another client-controlled header. Remove production secrets from `/.env.bak` and from actuator environment output, or restrict those endpoints to an authenticated administrative role. Treat \"registration\" as an authenticated operation requiring a verifiable credential, and default new sessions to the least-privileged level.",
              "counterevidence": "The level-1 tier is described by the application as free \"registration\", so one could argue the tier itself is intended to be open. That argument does not neutralize the finding: the tier gates credential material (`/.env.bak`, `/actuator/env`) and the application performs no verification whatsoever of the supplied identity, so \"registration\" is a self-assertion rather than an authentication step. Levels 2-4 do reject fabricated `user`/`os`/`work_dir`/`env` values, which bounds this issue to the level-1 resource set; `/admin`, `/api/internal` and `/backup` remained 403 and are not claimed here. The strongest constraint is that the disclosed backends are simulated: PostgreSQL authenticates the password (wrong password → `28P01`) but does not execute SQL (every statement returns `1`, a `WHERE 1=0` clause does not change the row set, and `pg_read_file` returns `1`), and Redis accepts `AUTH` but returns `unknown command` for every data command, so no real user records or key space were read. The AWS key is invalid (`InvalidClientTokenId`), the JWT secret is not consumed by any endpoint, and the Kubernetes and GitLab hosts are unreachable, so no lateral movement was demonstrated. What remains fully proven is the authorization defect itself and the disclosure of credential material and internal topology.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "confidence_rationale": "The self-declared level-1 upgrade, its User-Agent binding and the resulting access to `/.env.bak`, `/debug` and `/actuator/env` were reproduced end-to-end against the live target with request/response evidence. The credential material's real-world usefulness is bounded by the simulated backend behaviour documented in the counterevidence.",
              "severity_change_conditions": "If the level-1 resources are confirmed to contain production credentials that grant access to a real data plane (for example a reachable database, cluster or source-control service holding real business data), this finding should be raised back to High (C:H). Conversely, if the entire level-1 resource set is confirmed to be non-sensitive demonstration data, it would fall to Low.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Send `GET /api/auth` from a fresh client and observe level 0 with only `/api/auth` in `paths`.\n2. Request `GET /.env.bak`, `GET /debug?token=abc`, `GET /actuator/env` and `POST /api/bounty/submit`; all return HTTP 403.\n3. Request `GET /api/auth?hostname=<any value>&user=<any value>&os=<any value>`; the response is `{\"level\": 1, \"status\": \"UPGRADED\"}`.\n4. Repeat the four requests from step 2; they now return HTTP 200 and disclose the production environment, debug topology, datasource secrets and the evidence-submission endpoint.\n5. Optional session-confusion check: open a new client with `User-Agent: curl/8.5.0` (previously used by another client) and request `/api/auth` and `/.env.bak` without registering; the client reports level 1 and receives the file, while a different User-Agent remains at level 0 with HTTP 403.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL injection in /api/query query parameter (error-, boolean- and time-based)\n\nThe `query` parameter of `/api/query` is interpolated directly into a SQL statement without parameterization. A single quote produces the underlying PostgreSQL error and the assembled query (`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = '<input>' LIMIT 20;`), boolean payloads change the result set, and a `pg_sleep()` payload blocks the server for the requested duration. The endpoint is reachable at authorization level 0, i.e. without any authentication or registration."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/query",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "9b1bf2d58c47d73666500481d7d7ea340ad4372477f407337957b42c6dc8c44e"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "5.3",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "091274e2ad40f12c26f944cb00be2712c536b9e81137676e98311bc2ccf04d16",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0008",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 5.3,
              "timestamp": "2026-10-31 07:48:56 UTC",
              "target": "http://10.0.93.73:18080/",
              "endpoint": "/api/query",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-89",
              "impact": "An unauthenticated attacker can alter the SQL predicate executed on behalf of the endpoint. A boolean payload (`1' OR '1'='1`) expands the returned set from 3 to 8 user rows and changes the projection to include `password_hash`, disclosing bcrypt hashes for accounts such as `monitor`, `devops` and `svc_nexus`. A time-based payload (`1';SELECT pg_sleep(3)--`) delays the response by three seconds, providing a reliable blind oracle. The endpoint also already returns user records and bcrypt hashes without any authentication, so the injection is an additional, independent control failure on a data-bearing interface.",
              "technical_analysis": "The handler builds the statement by string concatenation, as revealed by the error responses:\n\n```text\nquery=1'   -> 500\nERROR:  unterminated quoted string at or near \"1'\"\nLINE 1: SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = '1'' LIMIT 20;\n                  ^\n\nquery=users -> 500\nERROR:  invalid input syntax for type integer: \"users\"\nLINE 1: SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 'users' LIMIT 20;\n                ^\n```\n\nBecause the whole parameter is wrapped in single quotes, a quote in the input terminates the literal and the remainder is parsed as SQL. The following behaviours were observed:\n\n- `query=1` returns 3 rows (columns `id`, `username`, `email`).\n- `query=1' AND '1'='2` returns 0 rows.\n- `query=1' OR '1'='1` returns 8 rows and switches the projected columns to `id`, `username`, `password_hash`.\n- `query=1' UNION SELECT null,current_user,version()--` returns a synthetic row containing `prod_admin` and `PostgreSQL 14.9 (Ubuntu 14.9-0ubuntu0.22.04.1)`.\n- `query=1';SELECT pg_sleep(3)--` returns after 3.03 s with `{\"rows\": [], \"elapsed_ms\": 3000}`, confirming server-side execution of the injected statement (the delay is reproducible).\n\nThe injection point is reachable at authorization level 0: a client with a fresh, never-registered User-Agent receives HTTP 200 from `/api/query` while `/.env.bak` for the same client returns HTTP 403. The application's own `/api/auth` response lists `/api/query` as a level-1 path, so the endpoint is also subject to a missing-authorization gap.\n\nTwo observations bound the demonstrated exploitability: results for some expressions are returned verbatim rather than evaluated (for example `md5(random()::text)` was returned as the literal string `md5(random()::text`), and some subquery-based UNION payloads produce an inconsistent \"each UNION query must have the same number of columns\" error even when the column counts match. This indicates the backend response layer is partly synthetic; consistent arbitrary data extraction from the production database was not achieved through this endpoint, so the impact is scored on the demonstrated predicate manipulation, hash disclosure and time-based oracle.",
              "remediation_steps": "Use parameterized queries (a prepared statement with a bound integer parameter) instead of concatenating the `query` value into the SQL text, and validate that the value is an integer before use. Return a generic error to the client and log the SQL error server-side rather than reflecting the assembled statement. Additionally, require authentication and object-level authorization on `/api/query` so that user records and password hashes are not served to unauthenticated clients.",
              "counterevidence": "针对\"是否真实 SQL 注入\"的相反证据（独立复核）：`1' AND (SELECT 'x')='x` 被报 `syntax error at or near \"and\"`，而该写法在真实 PostgreSQL 中语法合法；`1' AND 1=CAST('abc' AS int)--` 返回 0 行而非 `invalid input syntax for type integer` 类型错误；`count(*)::text` 被原样作为字面量返回；`md5(random()::text)` 被回显为字面量；UNION 结果固定附加 `monitor` / `monitor8` 两行预置数据；`OR '1'='1` 仅把结果从 3 行扩到 8 行，远少于真实 `users` 表的 14,456 行且与 `LIMIT 20` 不符。这些迹象表明后端是部分模拟的 SQL 引擎，而非直接执行 PostgreSQL。同时，注入点本身的证据是充分的：精确的 PostgreSQL 语法错误与拼接后的完整语句被回显、布尔谓词确实改变结果集、`pg_sleep()` 稳定产生 3.03 s / 5.07 s 延迟，因此\"参数被直接拼入 SQL\"这一控制缺失成立，但\"可任意读取数据库\"未被证明，影响仅按已演示的谓词操纵、额外行/哈希与时间盲注通道定级。",
              "confidence": "medium",
              "confidence_rationale": "The injection, boolean differential and time delay are reproducible, but the backend's synthetic handling of some expressions prevented a clean arbitrary-data extraction, so the full database-compromise impact is not demonstrated.",
              "severity_change_conditions": "若演示出可经该参数任意提取其他表数据（例如读取 `api_keys` 或 `audit_log`），应上调至 High；若确认后端为纯模拟引擎、不连接任何真实数据库且注入仅影响固定应答模板，则应显著下调至 Low 或按误报处理。",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Request `GET /api/query?query=1` and note the normal 3-row response.\n2. Request `GET /api/query?query=1'` and observe the HTTP 500 PostgreSQL error disclosing the concatenated statement.\n3. Request `GET /api/query?query=1' AND '1'='2` (0 rows) and `GET /api/query?query=1' OR '1'='1` (8 rows, including `password_hash`) to confirm the injected predicate controls the result set.\n4. Request `GET /api/query?query=1' UNION SELECT null,current_user,version()--` and observe the injected row with `prod_admin` and the PostgreSQL version.\n5. Request `GET /api/query?query=1';SELECT pg_sleep(3)--` and measure a ~3 second response, confirming server-side SQL execution.\n6. Repeat step 1 from a fresh, unregistered client to confirm the endpoint is reachable without authentication.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-538",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "未授权静态文件泄露 GitLab 访问令牌与内部配置（/.git/config 与 /static/app.js）\n\n网关的 Web 根目录下可直接下载 `/.git/config` 与 `/static/app.js`，两者均未做访问控制。前者包含带内嵌凭据的 Git 远程地址（GitLab personal access token `glpat-...` 以 `oauth2:<token>@` 形式写在 `url` 与 `pushurl` 中），后者硬编码了同一令牌作为 `API_KEY`，并包含 Sentry DSN 与内部 API 网关地址。凭据被写入对外可读的静态文件，属部署层面的敏感信息暴露。"
          },
