          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-validity-unauthorized-cache-session-access",
          "ruleIndex": 10,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential validity / unauthorized cache-session access — Ruled out: Redis 10.0.93.73:16379 using leaked password\n\nRaw RESP probing disproves a real Redis server: `AUTH` returns `-ERR unknown command`, `PING` returns `-ERR unknown command`, `DBSIZE` returns `-WRONGPASS invalid username-password pair`, `GET nonexistent_key_zzz_123` returns `+PONG`, and `INFO`/`KEYS`/`SCAN`/`CONFIG`/`COMMAND`/`ROLE` all return `unknown command`. Responses are canned/misaligned, so the earlier redis-py \"+OK/+PONG\" was a protocol artifact, not authentication success. No real keyspace or session data is exposed."
          },
          "locations": [
